      "id": "claim_656eda326e6e4801992a272ab5f88dbb",
      "statement": "The Rust backend consists of core modules in src-tauri/src/ including lib.rs (command registration and Tauri app setup), main.rs (entry point), types.rs (shared type definitions with TypeScript export via ts-rs), diff.rs (Myers diff algorithm), merge.rs (three-way merge), highlight.rs (syntect-based syntax highlighting), history.rs (history entry descriptions), limits.rs (input validation), store.rs (local JSON persistence with atomic writes), export.rs (diff formatting), language.rs (language detection), and markers.rs (diff change markers for minimap).",
